## General Overview of the Project
The task is to develop an online shopping center web application that allows users to browse products, manage their shopping carts, and process checkout procedures without using SQL for data storage.

## Software Functional Requirements
1. Users shall be able to log in by entering a username and password on the Login Page.
2. Users shall be able to register a new account by providing a username, password, and email on the Registration Page.
3. Users shall be able to browse the product list on the Product Listing Page, with each product having an option to add it to the shopping cart.
4. Users shall be able to view the contents of their shopping cart on the Shopping Cart Page.
5. Users shall be able to remove items from their shopping cart on the Shopping Cart Page.
6. Users shall be able to proceed to checkout by clicking the Checkout button on the Shopping Cart Page.
7. Users shall be able to enter their shipping address and payment information on the Checkout Page.
8. Users shall be able to confirm and finalize their order on the Checkout Page.
9. Users shall be able to view an order summary on the Order Confirmation Page, detailing their order.
10. Users shall be able to navigate back to the Product Listing Page from the Order Confirmation Page to continue shopping.

## Language
Use HTML and Python to develop a web application. You should use HTML to generate the web template by yourself.

## Data Storage
Data will be stored in local text files. Different types of data will be stored in separate `.txt` files. You should define the text file by yourself in advance. This structured data storage will facilitate easy data retrieval and management through simple file manipulations in Python, ensuring the application remains light and efficient without the need for a SQL database.

